- `ADD_TEST BerremanTests.MeasurementPlannerTests`

**How to implement.** The Planner reproduces the existing facts over their own designs (001 §M 'Acceptance — the planner reproduces existing facts. Their designs and helpers are reused; no new physics test is written': 'C1 is completely blind to g33, which is why a second crystal cut is required', 'C1 alone cannot determine three of the four constants, which is why the design needs more cuts', 'the cuts buy the gyration DIAGONAL and only the tilt buys its OFF-DIAGONAL'; the S14.1 brief 'The facts live in BerremanTests (a new planner class) beside the designs they reuse'). No forward solve and no fit runs: each fact reads a design (steps 473, 474) as looks through `plannerLookWith FullMuellerReach` (step 467; the designs are full Mueller observations) and asks `structuralReport` (step 469) about every parameter of its record. New `Berreman/BerremanTests/MeasurementPlannerTests.fs`: `type MeasurementPlannerTests()` in `namespace BerremanTests`, a class as its neighbours are, appended at the end of `BerremanTests.fsproj`'s compile `ItemGroup` with no comment. Class doc, one to three lines: the Measurement Planner's layer-1 report over spec 0044's own designs reproduces their ablation facts (spec 0050 S14.1). It opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain` with `CrystalPhysics`, `MuellerInverse`, `Studies` (`parameterAxes`), `PlannerSymmetry`, `MeasurementPlanner` and `ItemModels`, `BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness` (`expectOk`, step 335) and the `BerremanTestSupport` namespace; it names each design by its module (`QuartzSample.c1`, `BiaxialDesign.normalIncidenceOn`, `BiaxialSample.triclinic`) rather than opening them, because `configuration`, `fullConfigurations` and the plates share names across them. A private helper of the class, documented in one line, is `reportOver (crystal : CrystalParameters) (design : MeasurementConfiguration list) : RecoverabilityReport`: `crystal.structuralReport` of the names of `crystal.parameterAxes` (step 361) over the design's looks, through `expectOk`. Each fact compares `ParameterName`s, reasons, remedies and findings with `Assert.Equal` and names the report's finding texts in its failure messages. `the planner finds C1 blind to g33, leaves three of the four quartz constants unrecoverable and proposes the second cut`: over `UniaxialCrystal QuartzSample.quartz` and `QuartzSample.c1`, the report's `unrecoverable` names are [n_o; n_e; g33] and `reachable` [g11]; g33's finding has `AlongEveryPropagationReason` and n_o's `NoRetardanceReason`; each of the three has the remedies `[ AddPlateRemedy XCut; ObliqueIncidenceRemedy cap ]`, cap being `internalAngle QuartzSample.quartzOrdinaryIndex IncidenceAngle.maxValue` (`MuellerInverse.fs:internalAngle`; 40.40 degrees); and `offAxisCutOpt` is `Some { targets = [ n_e; g33 ]; capAngle = cap; cuts = [ XCut ] }`, the second cut. `the planner finds every quartz constant reachable once the second cut joins C1, and over the full C1-C4 set`: over `QuartzSample.c1 @ QuartzSample.c3` (the cut restored in `C1 alone cannot determine three of the four constants`) and over `QuartzSample.fullConfigurations` (`the full measurement set is well conditioned and every parameter is observable`), every parameter is reachable and there is no finding. `the planner flags g12, g13 and g23 for a normal-incidence-only biaxial design and names oblique incidence and further cuts as the remedy`: over `TriclinicCrystal BiaxialSample.triclinic` and `BiaxialDesign.normalIncidenceOn ZCut`, the `unrecoverable` names are [n3; g33; g23; g13; g12]: g23, g13 and g12 have `NormalIncidenceOnlyReason` and `[ ObliqueIncidenceRemedy cap ]` alone, cap being `internalAngle BiaxialSample.index1 IncidenceAngle.maxValue` (its smallest index), while n3 and g33 have `AlongEveryPropagationReason` and `[ AddPlateRemedy XCut; AddPlateRemedy YCut; ObliqueIncidenceRemedy cap ]`, and the off-axis finding names [n3; g33] with the cuts [XCut; YCut]: oblique incidence and further cuts; over that design followed by `normalIncidenceOn XCut`, and over `BiaxialDesign.b1` (every principal cut at normal incidence), the `unrecoverable` names are exactly [g23; g13; g12], each with the oblique remedy alone, and there is no off-axis finding: cutting more plates does not substitute for tilting them. `the planner finds all nine biaxial constants reachable over the full biaxial measurement set`: over `BiaxialDesign.fullConfigurations` every one of the nine parameters is reachable and there is no finding.

**Acceptance.** After the facts land, the Planner's structural report MUST find C1 blind to g33 with three of the four quartz constants unrecoverable and propose the x-cut, MUST flag g12, g13 and g23 for the normal-incidence biaxial designs with oblique incidence (and, for the z-cut alone, further cuts) as the remedy, and MUST find every constant reachable over the full designs; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class `BerremanTests.MeasurementPlannerTests`, including `the planner finds C1 blind to g33, leaves three of the four quartz constants unrecoverable and proposes the second cut`, `the planner finds every quartz constant reachable once the second cut joins C1, and over the full C1-C4 set`, `the planner flags g12, g13 and g23 for a normal-incidence-only biaxial design and names oblique incidence and further cuts as the remedy` and `the planner finds all nine biaxial constants reachable over the full biaxial measurement set`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s45 invariants MUST pass.
